# Soft-mask vs reward

Soft-mask = **look at / sample these rows** (train logit bias). It is **not** a good/bad label and does **not** mean “this pays.”

| Knob | Job | Not |
|------|-----|-----|
| Soft-mask (`softMaskLegal` / `soft_mask_legal`) | Attention / exposure — “consider these” (PASS **and** intentional fail distractors) | A reward, a grade, or “preferred = correct” |
| Reward (env ±, curriculum slap/bonus) | Good/bad after the look — “you looked; that was wrong/right” | A substitute for soft-mask exposure |

LOOSE_BALL_RUN TRAIN openings soft-mask pickup **plus** a few empty-EZ fails on purpose: force the look, then grade with reward. Do not argue that fail soft-masks “teach the net empty-EZ is good” — that confuses sampling tilt with reward. Critique fail soft-masks only as a **sampling/exposure** design choice, never as if they were the grade signal.
